          "label": "Anchor · conclusion",
          "voice": "Microsoft Zira Desktop",
          "visual": "closing",
          "title": "The crossing failed. The party survived.",
          "headline": "TWO IDEAS EXPLAIN THE STORY",
          "points": [
            "Adapt plans when conditions change",
            "Connect people’s skills to a shared goal"
          ],
          "credit": "Scope: the 28-person Endurance party · the separate Ross Sea party suffered losses",
          "narration": [
            "The remaining Endurance party was rescued from Elephant Island in August 1916. All twenty-eight members of that party survived.",
            "The wider expedition also included a separate Ross Sea party, which suffered losses, so we must be precise about whom we mean.",
            "The planned crossing was not completed. The rescue was a different achievement.",
